  "id": "COMPOUND:35798 - PROTEIN:519",
  "verbalization": "Ballonigrin is shown to have a target relationship with Protein-arginine deiminase type-3 through multiple pathways, all of which involve Protein-arginine deiminase type-1 as a intermediate. The evidence suggests that Ballonigrin may inhibit Protein-arginine deiminase type-1, which in turn targets several structurally related compounds, including (E)-4-[(1R,6R)-1-hydroxy-2,2,6-trimethyl-6-[(2S,3R,4R,5R,6R)-3,4,5-trihydroxy-6-(hydroxymethyl)oxan-2-yl]oxycyclohexyl]but-3-en-2-one, 1,1-Dimethoxycyclohexane, and 1,1,2-Trimethyl-3,5-bis(1-methylethenyl)cyclohexane. These compounds are all known to target Protein-arginine deiminase type-3, indicating a potential pathway where Ballonigrin may exert its effect through the inhibition of Protein-arginine deiminase type-1, which in turn affects the activity of multiple substrates of this enzyme. The consistent presence of Protein-arginine deiminase type-1 as a common target across these pathways supports the hypothesis that Ballonigrin may act through a mechanism involving the inhibition of this enzyme, potentially modulating the activity of its downstream targets. The evidence is robust and suggests a mechanistic link between Ballonigrin and Protein-arginine deiminase type-3, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact mode of action and the role of the intermediates.",
